WEBVTT

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.280
THIS IS THE TRUE FORM
OF EVANGELION: DEATH.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.740
2000 A.D., ANTARCTICA

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.460
<i>You're talking about Dr. Katsuragi's</i>
<i>Super Solenoid Theory?</i>

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.380
<i>I must say,</i>
<i>that theory is far too radical.</i>

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.500
<i>It's still very much a hypothesis.</i>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.130
<i>But the S2 theory is the only explanation</i>
<i>for how that giant is being powered.</i>

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.800
<i>There is no need to validate</i>
<i>what is already proven.</i>

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.310
<i>It exists right before us.</i>

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.520
-<i>We must accept it.</i>
<i>-Once all the data is in.</i>

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.940
<i>Scientists put far too much faith</i>
<i>in their beliefs.</i>

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.650
<i>You think they are dogmatic?</i>

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.070
<i>Their assumptions</i>
<i>are too deeply ingrained.</i>

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:57.530
<i>These are people who are unable</i>
<i>to accurately perceive reality.</i>

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:01.620
<i>And yet such people</i>
<i>seek the truth. How ironic.</i>

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.490
<i>There is nothing noble about what they do.</i>

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.080
<i>The act of discovery brings them joy,</i>
<i>and understanding leads to dominance.</i>

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.590
<i>What they seek is self-gratification,</i>
<i>nothing more.</i>

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.170
<i>Stop the surface luminescence!</i>
<i>It's exceeding threshold values!</i>

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.970
<i>The DNA that was inserted into Adam</i>
<i>has undergone physical fusion!</i>

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:22.720
<i>All the AT Fields are giving way!</i>

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.470
<i>-The spear! Pull up the spear!</i>
-<i>No-go! Magnetic field unstable!</i>

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.390
<i>It's sinking in!</i>

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.650
<i>Limit the damage any way you can!</i>
<i>Every bit counts!</i>

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.440
<i>Break up its component atoms</i>
<i>on the quark level! Hurry!</i>

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.650
<i>Initiate cooling cycle when</i>
<i>the Gates of Guf open!</i>

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:39.700
<i>Make it give off energy</i>
<i>that will interfere with</i>

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.200
<i>its own Anti-A.T. Field,</i>
<i>even for 0.1 seconds!</i>

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:44.620
<i>-Countdown in progress.</i>
<i>-It's spreading its wings!</i>

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.990
<i>It's reached the surface!</i>

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:07.680
Father...

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.660
FIFTEEN YEARS LATER,
SHE WAS IN BED WITH A MAN

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:33.250
I bet Ritsuko is looking down
her nose at me

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.630
right about now, thinking I'm indecent.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.590
You're truer to the human condition
when you indulge your desires.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.170
The deception should hold for a while.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.760
Against who, NERV Intelligence?
Or Commander Ikari or Ritsuko?

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:46.930
Or do you mean me?

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.310
No, yourself.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.310
"Others," don't you mean?

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.150
You're not all that interested in others,
but you always feel lonely.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.110
You really <i>are</i> like my father.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:00.990
NINE MONTHS AGO,
HE WAS GAZING AT THE STARS

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:05.620
Aw, we'll be in Japan tomorrow.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.490
Misato said she'd be there
by noon to pick me up.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.660
Darn, we'll be going
our separate ways for a while.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.120
This sucks.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.790
When we get there, I'm sure that lots
of new boyfriends will be waiting for you.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:19.960
And from what I hear,
the Third Children is a boy.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.630
I'm not interested in some dumb kid!

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.300
The only person I like is you, Mr. Kaji.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:27.260
SEVEN YEARS AGO,
SHE BURST THROUGH THE DOOR

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.770
Mommy! Mommy! I've been chosen!

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:34.440
I'm gonna be an elite pilot
that protects humanity!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.020
I'm the world's greatest!

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.570
It's supposed to be secret!
But I'll share it just with you, Mommy!

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.570
Lots of people are gonna be nice to me!
So I won't be lonely!

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:50.290
So I'll be fine even without Daddy!
I won't be lonely at all!

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.460
So look! Look at me!

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.040
Did you hear me, Mommy?

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:03.340
<i>Asuka, can you hear me?</i>
<i>Your synch rate is down by eight.</i>

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.430
<i>Keep all extraneous thoughts</i>
<i>from your mind.</i>

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:07.140
I'm trying to!

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:11.890
Asuka's synch rate has been
dropping steadily lately.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.520
This is the last thing we need
on top of everything else.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.310
Let's prioritize repairing Rei's Unit 00.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.190
Director.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.070
Good morning.
You have your son with you today?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.780
Oh, I thought you had a boy.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:29.240
This isn't Shinji.
I'm looking after a friend's daughter.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.240
Her name is Rei Ayanami.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.160
Hi there, Rei.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.790
FIVE YEARS LATER,
SHE MET HIM AGAIN

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.630
I can't reach her? I shouldn't have come.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.000
That's that, then.
Might as well head to a shelter.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.270
Don't run away...

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.940
A FEW MONTHS LATER,
HE WAS FACED WITH A DECISION

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:48.030
Thank you, Shinji.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.950
Kaworu, why are you--

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:55.700
It's my fate. It dictates that I live on.
Even if mankind perishes as a result.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:01.500
But I can die here if I want.
Life and death hold equal value to me.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.210
Choosing to die is the one
absolute freedom.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:11.680
What's that mean? Kaworu, I don't
understand what you're saying!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.140
They're my last words.

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.010
Now, go ahead and destroy me.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.850
If you don't,
you and your kind will disappear.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:24.310
Only one lifeform can avoid extinction
and be granted a future.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:25.730
EIGHTEEN MONTHS AGO...

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:35.490
TOKYO-2 (FORMERLY MATSUMOTO)
NAGANO PREFECTURE

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.240
NO.3 JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL AUDITORIUM

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:41.750
TWENTY-TWO MINUTES BEFORE
STRING QUARTET RECITAL PRACTICE

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.380
CELLO, THE FOURTH PLAYER

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:54.890
TUNING

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:46.440
<i>-Prepare for launch!</i>
<i>-Preparing Eva-01 for launch!</i>

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.770
<i>Main power connected!</i>

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.940
-<i>Release lockdown bolt no.1!</i>
-<i>Initiating umbilical bridge retraction!</i>

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:56.820
<i>Retracting primary restraining frame.</i>
<i>Removing secondary frame, as well.</i>

00:08:57.820 --> 00:09:00.410
<i>Roger. Transport Eva-01 to launch bay.</i>

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.540
TEST TYPE
EVA-01

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:03.410
<i>Launch preparations complete!</i>

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:04.960
Launch!

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.630
FIRST MISSION

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:18.050
Release final safeties!
Evangelion Unit 01, lift off!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.270
FIRST ACTIVATION

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:25.100
-Where are its defensive systems?!
-Signal inactive.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:26.560
Field not raised!

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.350
It's not working?

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.360
CRANIAL INJURY

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.700
HEMORRHAGE

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.490
-Sit-rep!
-Skull damage, severity unknown!

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:40.740
<i>-Operational integrity compromised!</i>
-Pilot readings lost!

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.370
No luck! System is
completely unresponsive!

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.120
It's what?!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Has it gone...

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:50.500
REACTIVATION

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:54.960
...berserk?!

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:09.980
We've won.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.030
An A.T. Field!

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:18.320
Unit 01's also raised an A.T. Field!
Phase space is being neutralized!

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:20.070
No, it's <i>corroding</i> it.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.370
THREAT

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.000
NO CONTROL

00:10:34.380 --> 00:10:35.590
HEMORRHAGE

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.300
1ST BATTLE ABOVE NERV HQ

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.640
CLOSE QUARTERS COMBAT

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.180
RUPTURE / SLAUGHTER

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:49.100
SLAUGHTER

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.190
TERROR / FEAR

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:53.110
DEATH THROES

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:57.530
EXPLOSION

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.420
-That's the Evas'...
-...true nature.

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.510
I think your boxes of stuff
are already here.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.970
Actually, I only moved here
recently, myself.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.060
Come on in!

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:31.310
Uh, thanks for having me...

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.860
Shinji, this is your home.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:42.950
I-- I'm home.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.370
Welcome back.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:46.450
Who is she?

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:48.750
The sole survivor
of the original expedition.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.830
She hasn't spoken a single word
in nearly two years.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:54.250
That poor girl.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.420
Whatever she saw,
it was bad enough to do that.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:01.840
Mental trauma can take longer to heal
than simple physical injuries.

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:04.720
-Her name is...
-Ms. Katsuragi?

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.390
Yep! Misato Katsuragi!
Pleased to meet'cha!

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:10.480
<i>Mother, I met a girl named</i>
<i>Katsuragi the other day.</i>

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:14.310
<i>I learned that she was the sole survivor</i>
<i>of that doomed expedition.</i>

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.770
<i>She says she suffered from aphasia,</i>
<i>unable to speak for a while,</i>

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.530
<i>but the way she goes on and on now,</i>
<i>it's like she's making up for lost time.</i>

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:26.160
<i>Do I want to be a good girl?</i>
<i>I need to be a good girl.</i>

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.740
<i>Because Daddy is always gone.</i>

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:33.210
<i>I need to be a good girl and help Mommy.</i>

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:36.960
<i>But I don't want to end up like Mommy.</i>

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:41.590
<i>Because Mommy is always crying</i>
<i>when Daddy is away.</i>

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.800
<i>I shouldn't cry. I shouldn't act spoiled.</i>

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.640
<i>That's why I need to be a good girl.</i>

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.270
<i>But I hate my father.</i>
<i>That's why I hate being a good girl.</i>

00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.520
<i>I hate it... I'm tired.</i>

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.190
Yes, ma'am.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:13:02.070
Oh, Misato is the person NERV sent
to Germany before you, Mr. Kaji.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:05.860
I don't like her that much.
She's always putting up a front.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.870
<i>Ms. Misato Katsuragi...</i>

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:12.080
-<i>She's not a bad person.</i>
-<i>Good morning, Shinji...</i>

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.830
I've been through so much
since I got here.

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.580
Before this, I was staying with a teacher.

00:13:17.670 --> 00:13:19.840
Days there were quiet and uneventful.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.260
All I did was take up space.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:25.510
But that was fine with me.
There was nothing that I wanted to do.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.890
I had nothing that I wanted to live for.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.640
You hate being around other people?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.310
Not exactly.
I don't think I cared either way.

00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:39.900
But I did hate my father.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:44.690
I'm amazed that Shinji was willing
to go through with this.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:49.200
He does whatever he's told.
That's how he makes his life easier.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.620
Center the target, pull the trigger.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.000
Center the target, pull the trigger.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.830
Center the target, pull the trigger.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.310
Don't run away. Don't run away.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.850
Don't run away. Don't run away.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:30.740
<i>Today, the Fourth Angel attacked</i>
<i>from out of the clear blue sky.</i>

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:34.240
<i>Unit 01 intercepted the Angel</i>
<i>and narrowly managed to defeat it.</i>

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.910
Shinji, get up.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.120
How long are you gonna
stay home from school?

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.630
Unit 01 is as good as new.

00:14:41.710 --> 00:14:44.420
Its pilot shouldn't be
sitting around like this.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.260
Shinji?

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:52.550
TO MS. MISATO KATSURAGI

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.010
TOKYO-3 LOOP LINE NO.7

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:03.060
<i>It has been raining incessantly</i>
<i>for four days.</i>

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:07.740
<i>Poor weather is hindering</i>
<i>the dismantling of the Angel sample.</i>

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:12.320
<i>Nothing else of note to record today.</i>

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.920
<i>The sun finally came out today,</i>

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.590
<i>resulting in a day that was sunny,</i>
<i>but with intermittent clouds.</i>

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:31.130
<i>Nothing else of note</i>
<i>to record today, either.</i>

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.140
I like it at night.

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.140
Those cicadas aren't buzzing away.

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.650
It was nice and quiet when I was a kid,
but there's more every year.

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:48.360
Ms. Misato said something about
the ecosystem rebuilding itself.

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.240
"Ms. Misato," huh?

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:58.330
I'm so jealous! You live with a total babe
and you get to pilot that Evangelion.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.960
Your Eva is ready and waiting.
Will you pilot it?

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.170
Or not?

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.420
You're not going to scold me
for running away?

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:14.470
I guess you wouldn't. You're not family.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:21.520
What would happen with Unit 01
if I didn't pilot it?

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.980
I suppose Rei would pilot it.

00:16:25.190 --> 00:16:26.270
You're not going to?

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:32.280
How could I do something like that?
I couldn't force it all on her.

00:16:32.360 --> 00:16:34.780
Don't worry. I'll do it.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:36.490
But you don't want to?

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.750
Of course not.
I'm not cut out for this stuff.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.290
But you and Ayanami and Ms. Ritsuko--

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.580
Knock it off!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.880
What others think doesn't matter!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.090
If you don't like it, then leave!

00:16:50.210 --> 00:16:54.090
Forget about the Evas and everything else!
Go back to your old life!

00:16:55.970 --> 00:16:59.010
If you keep acting like this,
you're more trouble than you're worth!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:03.640
If you don't stick around, we'll all
probably have to leave town eventually.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:06.480
But we can't force you to stay.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:09.730
We saw what it's like for you in that Eva.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:14.110
I dare anybody to bad-mouth you!
I'll beat the crap out of the guy!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.950
I'm the one who should be clobbered!

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.990
I'm dishonest! And a coward!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:22.540
I'm a sneak! And a weakling...

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.870
Don't run away, Shinji.

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:28.710
Not from your father,
and especially not from yourself.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:32.630
Are you sure, Shinji?

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.010
It's fine, I prefer being alone.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.180
It's all the same to me.

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:42.520
Wow! Buildings are sprouting
from the ground!

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:47.560
If you don't stick around, we'll all
probably have to leave town eventually.

00:17:47.650 --> 00:17:50.360
But we can't force you to stay.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:54.900
We saw what it's like for you in that Eva.

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.660
And... it's the city that you protected.

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:01.780
I forgot to tell you something:

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:06.370
People will thank you
for what you did today.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.370
You should be proud.

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:11.670
Good night, Shinji.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:13.300
Keep it up.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.990
<i>The Third Children had been suffering</i>
<i>from a temporary slump.</i>

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.200
<i>Most likely cause, burnout.</i>

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:48.460
<i>Was given four days R&R</i>
<i>to ensure proper recuperation.</i>

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.540
<i>Subject now healthy and back on duty.</i>

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:55.670
I... I'm back.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:18:58.260
Welcome home.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:03.140
-Good morning, Ikari.
-Hey, good morning.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.980
NO. 3 JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL AUDITORIUM

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:10.440
<i>I forget, what are we doing today?</i>

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:12.400
Pachelbel's "Canon."

00:19:12.480 --> 00:19:15.980
You have it so easy. The cello
just plays arpeggios in this piece.

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:18.070
SECOND VIOLIN,
THE SECOND PLAYER

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:20.360
TUNING

00:20:22.550 --> 00:20:23.720
Mommy...

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.430
Mommy...

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.650
You're just as much a kid as I am.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.270
<i>Hello, Misato.</i>

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:39.610
How have you been?

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.740
Not bad. Hey, have you grown in height?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.200
Yep. And I'm filling out
in all the right places, too.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:53.370
Allow me to introduce the Second Children,
Evangelion Unit 02's designated pilot.

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:55.670
Asuka Langley Soryu.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.500
<i>-Overbearing!</i>
<i>-Stuck up!</i>

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.420
<i>-Cocky!</i>
<i>-Weirdo!</i>

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.010
<i>-Self-centered!</i>
<i>-A showoff!</i>

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.630
<i>-A cold fish!</i>
<i>-Two-faced!</i>

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:06.840
-Baumkuchen!
<i>-Heartless!</i>

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.970
<i>-Thin-skinned!</i>
<i>-A real piece of work!</i>

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:11.600
<i>Rubs me the wrong way!</i>

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:17.730
<i>Are you afraid of intimacy with others?</i>

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:20.780
<i>If you avoid other people,</i>
<i>you'll never be betrayed.</i>

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:22.780
<i>You won't hurt each other, either.</i>

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:26.110
<i>But you'll also never stop feeling lonely.</i>

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:29.950
<i>Humans can't permanently</i>
<i>be free of loneliness.</i>

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.540
<i>Because man is ultimately alone.</i>

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:35.210
<i>But people can go on living</i>
<i>because they're able to forget.</i>

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.750
<i>The human heart is in constant pain.</i>

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:42.340
<i>The heart is sensitive to pain,</i>
<i>so that makes living feel painful.</i>

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.930
-So, what do you think of Shinji Ikari?
-He's a letdown.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:50.220
A guy like him, picked to be
the Third Children? I'm disillusioned.

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:54.390
He got tossed unprepared into a fight,
but his synch rate easily topped 40.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:56.810
Synchronization rate, zero.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:58.060
Third Children!

00:21:58.150 --> 00:22:00.650
No longer qualified as Second Children.

00:22:01.230 --> 00:22:02.230
Come with me for a minute.

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:06.900
Wow, Unit 02 is red. I had no idea.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:09.410
Unit 00 and 01 are really just

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:12.280
a developmental-use prototype
and test type.

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:16.750
The fact that you could synch with yours
without any training proves it.

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:19.120
But Unit 02 here is different!

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:24.670
Mine was built for combat operations,
the world's first <i>real </i>Evangelion!

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:26.380
It's the official type!

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:31.890
-What was that?
-An underwater shock wave!

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:34.100
That blast was nearby.

00:22:39.520 --> 00:22:40.730
ENEMY ATTACK

